Kontrol-ID manages Kontrol's standalone multithread secure web gateway for
transparent or explicit proxy access. Clients may use Windows endpoint
identification from the reusable Provisioner, intentionally anonymous default
and source-IP policy, or explicit proxy authentication. It provides native
Kerberos/SPNEGO, opt-in NTLMv2/Winbind, and HTTP Basic authentication through
the Kontrol local or LDAP server, assisted AD/keytab enrollment, policy-group
mapping, TLS inspection, a fallback login portal and XMLRPC synchronization.

The managed WPAD page publishes a syntax-validated PAC through the native
Kontrol nginx hook. It can own DHCP Option 252 and a DNS wpad host override,
and removes only the files and service records that it created.

No Squid process or persistent Kontrol service on Windows endpoints is required.
Kerberos is the recommended explicit authentication method; NTLMv2 is retained
for legacy domain clients and Basic is limited to trusted client networks.
